  "title": "The Sequel Before Scene One",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "creative-work struggles",
  "premise": "A storyteller wants to launch a ten-part saga, but every unfinished first scene splits into more sequel posters. They fold the posters into a small screening room, finish a self-contained first scene, and let the single audience member choose whether another poster comes down from storage.",
  "hook": "Episode twelve is ready. Episode one is a rectangle.",
  "visible_action": "Posters multiply along a wall; first-scene rectangle remains blank; posters fold into seats; one short scene plays; audience points at one future poster.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A complete small story can support what comes next.",
  "gate": "Use entirely original poster art; no claim that this approach guarantees audience growth.",
